[38;5;252m[1m## What the tests actually pin down[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The translation's value is in the quirks it preserves, and those are where I concentrated. The most consequential:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- In [38;5;10mtokenizer_next_token[0m, the comment test [38;5;10mc == '/' && (peek_char() == '/' || peek_char() == '*')[0m calls [38;5;10mpeek_char()[0m [3mbefore[23m advancing, so it still returns [38;5;10mc[0m. The condition collapses to [38;5;10mc == '/'[0m, meaning every slash becomes a [38;5;10mCOMMENT[0m token and [38;5;10mscan_operator[0m is dead code for [38;5;10m/[0m. A translation that read the [3mnext[23m character instead would diverge on token types, distribution counts and complexity scores.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcreate_token[0m computes [38;5;10mcurrent_column - token.length[0m as [38;5;10mint - size_t[0m, so the subtraction happens unsigned and truncates back to [38;5;10mint[0m — columns wrap negative for tokens at the start of a line.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10manalyze_text[0m overwrites the newline tally it just computed with the tokenizer's [3mcumulative[23m line total, which [38;5;10mtokenizer_reset[0m intentionally never clears, so "Lines:" grows across menu invocations.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mbreak[0m in main's cases 2 and 5 leaves the [38;5;10mswitch[0m, not the [38;5;10mwhile[0m, so EOF at those prompts reprints the whole menu.[0m[0m
- A 255-byte input line makes [38;5;10mfgets[0m leave the newline behind, so the next read returns bare [38;5;10m"\n"[0m and silently ends the input block.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/ERRORS.md[0m records all 13 audited quirks with the C construct, the behavior, and the test that covers it, plus the six paths no input can reach ([38;5;10mtokenizer_peek_token[0m, the uninitialized-analyzer error, [38;5;10mTOKEN_WORD[0m, and others).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One judgment call worth flagging: for an unseekable file such as a FIFO or [38;5;10m/dev/stdin[0m, the C reaches genuine UB — [38;5;10mftell[0m returns -1, then [38;5;10mfread(content, 1, (size_t)-1, file)[0m runs against a [38;5;10mmalloc(0)[0m buffer. Both binaries produced identical output when I ran them, but I deliberately did not encode that as an assertion, since a UB outcome isn't a specification worth locking in. [38;5;10m/proc/version[0m is asserted instead, because that path (stat size 0, nothing read) is well defined.[0m[0m
